se provided toFast Company, multitudes of instruments have monitored the Moon’s surface for decades, and the new Lunar Foundation Model will help researchers analyze it all, get a sense of how the surface is changing, and, in short, better prepare for new missions to the Moon.Ultimately, what the tool can do is help astronauts eventually navigate around the moon more safely, track down potential resources (such as ice deposits), and identify certain geological features that may present hazards.The last timehumans were on the Moon was in December 1972 as part of the Apollo 17 mission, but plans to return are underway—NASA’s Artemis Programintends to land a crewed mission on the lunar surfac...", "published_at": "2026-09-10T17:00:00+00:00", "image_url": null, "source": {"name": "Fast Company", "tier": "independent", "url": "https://www.fastcompany.com"}, "bias_scores": [{"political_lean": 35, "sensationalism": 20, "opinion_fact": 29, "factual_rigor": 31, "framing": 18, "confidence": 0.48, "rationale": {"lean": {"keyword_score": 50.0, "framing_shift": 0.0, "entity_shift": 0.0, "sentence_direction": 0.0, "text_score": 50.0, "source_baseline": 35, "text_shift": 0.0, "delta_max": 10, "confidence": 1.0, "top_left_keywords": [], "top_right_keywords": [], "framing_phrases_found": [], "entity_sentiments": {}, "state_affiliated": false, "unscored": false}, "sensationalism": {"headline_score": 1.1, "body_score": 12.7, "clickbait_signals": 0, "superlative_density": 0.0, "urgency_density": 0.0, "hyperbole_density": 0.0, "measured_density": 0.0, "partisan_attack_density": 0.0}, "opinion": {"pronoun_score": 0.0, "subjectivity_score": 27.4, "modal_score": 0.0, "hedging_score": 0.0, "attribution_score": 35.9, "metadata_score": 0.0, "value_judgment_score": 0.0, "absolutist_assertion_score": 0.0, "classification": "Analysis", "dominant_signals": ["attribution_gaps", "subjectivity"]}, "coverage": {"named_sources_count": 1, "org_citations_count": 3, "data_points_count": 0, "direct_quotes